The borrow checker rejected a mutable borrow while the map iterator still held an immutable reference. Collect the keys into Vec<String>, drop the iterator, then update the map.
```rust
let keys: Vec<_> = map.keys().cloned().collect();
for key in keys { map.get_mut(&key).unwrap().count += 1; }
```

The React menu uses roving tabIndex and handles ArrowDown, ArrowUp, Home, End and Escape. Focus moves between enabled items.
```tsx
const [active, setActive] = useState(0);
return items.map((x,i) => <button tabIndex={i===active?0:-1}>{x.label}</button>);
```
